# Globs no agent may edit without a human decision, in EVERY repository on this
# machine - registered or not. One per line, repo-relative, shell-style globs.
# A pattern with no slash matches by file name anywhere in the tree.
#
# Keep this list to things that are dangerous everywhere. Per-repository
# additions belong in the registry entry:
#   node scripts/repos.mjs list        (the "protected" field on an entry)
# Those are added to this list; they cannot weaken it.
#
# The CLI can enforce a second, coarser layer without a hook:
#   copilot --deny-tool='write(.env)'
# The hook is here because it gives the agent a reason it can act on.
.env
.env.*
**/secrets.*
**/*.pem
**/id_rsa
.github/workflows/**
infra/**
**/infra/**
migrations/**
**/migrations/**
